A||N||15||lildevil||Honda S2000's SUCK!||||13||
Z||000000||lildevil||08-27-2001||07:07 PM||||My brother and I went to the track Friday nite, and low and behold there was a Honda S2000 club there. For those that do not know, these are the new HOT thing from Honda, a two seat rear wheel drive convertible sports car. It has something like a 9000 rpm redline and 240 HP VTEC motor. According to Road and Track, these cars do the 1/4 mile in 14.1 seconds.<BR>I sat there and watched as one right after another ran 15.1-14.9. You would think it was driver error, but ALL 6 ran these times. During eliminations there dial ins were 15.0, everyone of them! They rolled in thinking they were the hot S**T and came away looking like fools!<BR>The only thing I can see as an explaination is simply they do not know how to drive their cars! Maybe they weren't shifting at the lofty redline. Any one else have any experience with these cars?<P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||13
Z||000001||DreXteR||08-27-2001||07:29 PM||||Personally I dont believe a S2000 are for 1/4 mille run. They must be for long race, like highway races or long distances where the 9rpms are shine. In 1/4 mile do you need brute power and for sure the S2000, Celica GTS and those 4 banger dont have it unless you modified it.<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||08-27-2001||07:35 PM||||We have an S2000 and I love it... I mean, it sounds way to much like a Honda, of course... what they say about the power at higher RPMs very very true. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||saleenfiero||08-27-2001||08:46 PM||||They should sound like a Honda.  Anybody not used to the high revvability of these cars would not understand the attraction to them.  I am not a big fan of them, but they can rev and I think that would be fun in a certain way.<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTZ34||08-27-2001||08:48 PM||||What about elevation, track surface, ambient/track temps, tire compound etc.  You get the picture.  I agree that the S2000 isn't really setup for drag.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||08-27-2001||08:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lildevil:<BR><B>My brother and I went to the track Friday nite, and low and behold there was a Honda S2000 club there. For those that do not know, these are the new HOT thing from Honda, a two seat rear wheel drive convertible sports car. It has something like a 9000 rpm redline and 240 HP VTEC motor. According to Road and Track, these cars do the 1/4 mile in 14.1 seconds.<BR>I sat there and watched as one right after another ran 15.1-14.9. You would think it was driver error, but ALL 6 ran these times. During eliminations there dial ins were 15.0, everyone of them! They rolled in thinking they were the hot S**T and came away looking like fools!<BR>The only thing I can see as an explaination is simply they do not know how to drive their cars! Maybe they weren't shifting at the lofty redline. Any one else have any experience with these cars?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Don't forget to add in the track conditions & track temp, humidity, air temp & elevation. I think it could be a 14 sec car if the conditions were right.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">          <BR></A>||||reg||14
Z||000006||88formula||08-27-2001||09:07 PM||||Honda S2000 suck? Yeah right!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||08-27-2001||09:15 PM||||I drove one, not in a drag race, the owner was with me and the car had less than 1000 miles on it.  It ran nice for what I'd want it for a fun two seater that can move, but you need to be at 6000 rpm for the feel of power.  It handled real nice...but at $34K  too much money.||||reg||1
Z||000008||lildevil||08-27-2001||10:06 PM||||first off i need to say that i didn't post the original reply. It was my brother  NOS3800. We share the same computer and he got loged in under my name before he relized it. I wouldn't say they suck. They would definitly eat my car for lunch in a back road race i am sure.  They are HANDLING cars. But they do SUCK as a Drag car. Any car that you have to beat the crap out of jus to get some decent times doesn't sound like any fun to me.  You should have smelt the burnt clutches when they pulled back in the pit area.  I even heard one of  the drivers complaining about their performance.  I think my brother had a problem with the owners arrogence and attitude more then anything. They rode in an looked at all the American Muscle( our cars included) a basically laughed and stuck their noses up in the air. Then they made their 15 sec runs...came back into the pits and saw the 13's on our windows and started making excuses.  Maybe its jus me but i can't stand the RICER attitude.<P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Slammed Fiero||08-27-2001||10:19 PM||||Got a chane to drive one a while back in an autocross<P>Twitchy.<BR>No low end TQ<BR>Had to rev the poo out of it to get it to go.<BR>No car I would rather over rev than a Honda though. The sound is more F1 like than anything. Their piston speeds approach that of an F1 car , nice engineering , but I found it to be light on the tail.<P>Setup right it could be a killer, But not for Drag racing.<P>Still a fun car. Felt faster than 15.0 neighbourhood though. Most people don't realize the concept of Vtec or howit works.. You need to really beat ont he motor to create any sort of power.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||08-27-2001||10:22 PM||||Car & Driver said pretty much the same thing. They're real road-burners, but the only way you can get decent 0-60 or quarter mile times is to drive 'em like you're mad at 'em. Wind it up and side step the clutch.<BR>I suspect that I could learn to live with one, though. If I just HAD to.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000011||NOS3800||08-27-2001||11:46 PM||||First I must apologize for writing this post under the wrong name. Anyway, like my brother said I did write the post good and mad. Their attitudes were SOOOOOO holier then thou. And that rubbed me the wrong way. As for conditios, it was at nite, their runs were at 11 PM and the temp was 60's. Humidity was supposed to be low, but the air felt sticky and condensation formed on our hoods and roof. But conditions were better then average I feel. <BR>My buddy(with a new Mustang GT) were talking when the 5 S200's pulled up behind us after their runs and they were scratching their heads. Well, we looked over and in the light from there headlights, there was all this smoke. We thought my buddies GT was smoking, but we smelled it and it was the burning clutches from the Hondas.<BR>I read in a magazine that in order to get the times they got(14.1) they had to rev the motor to 7500 rpm and drop the clutch! WOW! Who in their right mind would do that?<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.45@99.70 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000012||NOS3800||08-27-2001||11:48 PM||||elevation was a few hundred feet over sea level.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Alex4mula||08-28-2001||01:08 PM||||I saw one at the drag strip here and it ran around 14.2 to 14.5 with a lot of tire spin. Track elevation here is about 10-15ft above sea level. Temp. was in the 80s. Also saw a Focus running 7s! (v6 twin turbo beast).||||reg||1
Z||000014||artherd||08-29-2001||02:14 AM||||I've driven one, it has *nothing* below 6,000rpm or so.  Literally, nothing. I was expecting more from 2.0litres and vtec cams (supposed to provide one for lowend and another for top-end, no compromises.)<P>The car felt... poorly setup. It hunted, lurched in the turn-in. like it couldn't make up it's mind which way to go.<P>Still, all in all a fun car, as soon as the damn engine finally climbs it's revs.   this thing really needs a *LIGHTened* flywheel more than anything.<P>You really do have to drive it like you are mad at it though, not just wind it out higher than any other car, it's different. It feels like you shouldn't be doing this, like you *know* it's hurting the car, and you do it anyway. I don't know how well the engine is balanced, wether it's the rest of the car shaking, wether 4-cyls just vibrate inherantly, or what.<P>Maybe it just takes too damn long to get to redline, and you feel you should be two gears higher and back in the powerband already, I don't know.<P>Wheras in a 355/360 Ferrari, well, these machines, nay, works of art, just BEG you to let that 5-valve V8 SCREAM! Heh. I say a lot about these two cars, and I mean every word, they're great  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>Magical combination of both torque, AND an 8250rpm redline. And you get the rest of the car for free!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>I once talked with a gent who had just test driven an F355 F1. He was complaining that the shifts took too long, and that the car was slow.  I simply responted "Shift at 8,000"  After picking his chin off the ground, he went back, took a test drive, and came back to see me.  "HOLEY ****  THIS CAR WILL LIGHT THE TYRES IN THIRD AT 100 I LOVE IT I WANT ONE OH MY GOD!!!"  He bought one that day. (wish I had those kinds of impulse buy options  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000015||Kwez||08-30-2001||01:56 AM||||yeah, it seems to be a typical "I'm god, look at me" car.<BR>At a car show 2 summers ago (2000), a guy just like that was more or less laughing at our Subaru club ...<BR>until the autocross competition, top 3 places: Subarus ;-)<BR>I also saw a professional driver driving a Impreza TS beat an S2000 on a mirror autocross course.<BR>(it's all behind the wheel)<P>S2, 0-60 very low 5secs, BUT<BR>drop the clutch @ (only ;-)  6000rpm & shift @ 6000rpm ... 0-60 10secs !!!<P>I'm sure driven 'correctly' they can do wonders though<BR>and they look pretty dagn nice too<p>[This message has been edited by Kwez (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||6
